2026-09-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2232) 'RFD authoring as an Elixir DSL
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2232) 'An RFD is an Elixir module that uses `RFD.DSL`: one `rfd` block with `state`, `feature`, `scope`, `flight_level`, `decision`, `problem`, `references`, `related`, `details` sections and `drafted_by`. The block builds an `RFD.Doc` and validates it against RFD66606-1000 while the file compiles, so a state outside the list, a missing Decision or a README over 40 lines is a compile error that names the rule.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2232) '- RFD66606-1000, the shape
 # tags: rfd:references
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2232) '- RFD66606-2177, the flight_level tag on the register
 # tags: rfd:references
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The register and the render
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2232) 'A site's serial register is a module that uses `RFD.Register`: `allocated`, `unused` and `deleted` blocks of `serial`, `never_written` and `retired` rows. `mix rfd.render` writes README.md, DETAILS.md and `SERIALS*.usda`, the shape the gates and `pen-66606.usda` read, and those files are ignored by git.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2232) 'Why Elixir
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The taskweft domains beside many RFDs are already Elixir, so the authoring form that can refuse a malformed document before it is written is the language the repository already runs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The flight level
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2232) 'RFD66606-2177: the register carries `flight_level`, so the DSL writes it to the register row, not the README.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2232) 'Layout
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2232) 'One file per RFD, `rfd/NNNN-slug.exs`, rendered into `rfd/NNNN-slug/`. A directory exists in git only when it carries apparatus beside the document (a USD layer, a skill, a script); README.md, DETAILS.md and `index.md` under `rfd/` are build artifacts and `.gitignore` names them. The registers are `SERIALS.exs` (site 1, frozen) and `SERIALS-vsekai-fabric.exs` (site 2, where new serials come from), rendered to the `.usda` beside them. A new RFD is a new `.exs` and a new `serial` line in the site's `allocated` block; `mix rfd.serials` refuses a source with no row, a row with no source, a slug that disagrees with the file name, and a deleted serial that has a source.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2232) 'What the render is checked against
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2232) '`mix test` at the root runs the positive cases and the negative controls: an unknown state, a missing Decision, a 40-line overflow, a serial listed twice, a serial from another site, a retired row naming no serial, a renumbering and a revived serial are each refused. The rendered tree then passes `check-rfd-structure.py`, `check-rfd-serials.py`, `check_tropes.py` and `check_rfd_canary.py` unchanged, which is the compatibility claim: the DSL emits what the existing pipeline consumes. CI and the prek hooks render before any gate reads the tree, and the diff-based gates scope themselves by the changed `.exs` sources.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2232) 'What the conversion found
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2232) 'Importing 306 RFDs lost no line of prose (`mix rfd.import` refuses a lossy import). Importing the two registers refused four rows: serial 2143 named both `fdb-backup-fans-out-to-r2` on main and `close-out-gates-red-green-scout` from a merged branch, so the second took the next unused serial, 2233; serial 2169 was allocated and deleted at once; 2184 and 2186 carried slugs their directories had left behind; and 2232 had been appended into the deleted scope. A prose tell (an em-dash join, a pompous copula, an `exact` on a soft noun) in any field a reader sees is a compile error, like the other shape rules.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The MADR template as a block
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The seven MADR headings are a `madr` block rather than seven `details` strings: `context`, `drivers`, `options`, `outcome`, `consequences`, `confirmation`, `more_information`. The DSL owns the headings, so a spelling cannot drift, and it refuses a section given twice, a run out of the template's order, a block missing its context or its outcome, a second block and an empty one. A body is a string or a list of strings, and `consequences` also takes `good:` and `bad:` lists. `details/2` stays for a section outside the template, in declaration order beside the block. The RFDs that carry nothing but the template render the same bytes through it as they did through the strings. The block nests one level and `mix format` re-indents a heredoc to its call, so a file whose body lines already run past the formatter's `line_length` stays on `details` strings: RFD66606-2062 carries an inventory table of 124 such lines.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2232) 'Related RFDs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2232) 'RFD66606-1000 (the README limit and the spine), RFD66606-2177, RFD66606-2026 (commit style the rendered files ride on).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2232) 'What the DSL does not do
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2232) 'It does not read the register from the RFD sources: a serial is a fact the register records once, and a deleted serial has no source to derive it from. It does not write: the endpoint answers, and a change is a pull request.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-07T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2232) 'The register was a hand-edited layer nothing compiled: it carried one serial on two directories, one serial allocated and deleted at once, and two slugs that no longer matched their directories.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2232  1 LINE
 Text:Written

